claims.source_body:
[norm-factorised majorants]
\label{def:majclass}
A bound on the comb--comb term is \emph{norm-factorised} if there are a norm
$\mathcal N$ on $\R^{n}$ and a nondecreasing
$\Phi:[0,\infty)\to[0,\infty)$ with
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:majclass}
  |\det S|\;\le\;\Phi\bigl(\mathcal N(\varrho)\bigr)
  \qquad\text{for every admissible weight vector }\varrho .
\end{equation}
The class of all such bounds, over all norms and all nondecreasing $\Phi$, is
written $\mathfrak M$.

