claims.source_body:
[the placement response in closed form]
\label{prop:fh}
Let $\vartheta\mapsto G(\vartheta)$ be as in Lemma~\ref{lem:dcexact}, suppose
$\lmin(G)$ and $\lmax(G)$ are simple with unit eigenvectors $v$ and $w$, and
suppose $\ah_{11}\ah_{22}\ne0$ and $r_{12}^{2}\ne1$. Then, with
$R=\gamma/(1-r_{12}^{2})$ as in \eqref{eq:ratio},
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:fh}
  \frac{\mathrm d\log R}{\mathrm d\vartheta}
  =\frac{v^{\T}\dot Gv}{\lmin(G)}-\frac{w^{\T}\dot Gw}{\lmax(G)}
   -\frac{1}{1-r_{12}^{2}}\,
    \frac{\mathrm d\,(1-r_{12}^{2})}{\mathrm d\vartheta},
\end{equation}
where the last derivative is the closed expression
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:ddel}
  \frac{\mathrm d\,(1-r_{12}^{2})}{\mathrm d\vartheta}
  =-\frac{2\ah_{12}\dot a_{12}}{\ah_{11}\ah_{22}}
   +\frac{\ah_{12}^{2}}{\ah_{11}\ah_{22}}
    \Bigl(\frac{\dot a_{11}}{\ah_{11}}+\frac{\dot a_{22}}{\ah_{22}}\Bigr),
  \qquad \dot a_{ij}=t_i^{\T}\dot At_j .
\end{equation}
Every quantity on the right is an explicit finite sum; no fit enters.

